## T1 — the census reproduces exactly

I re-ran `census.py` myself: `universe=138 registry=128 prod_decorators=123 seed=127
migrations=68 throughput=126 parse_errors=0` — identical to the report. Cross-checked against my
own independent measurements: registry 128, seed 127 (my text-parse in V-12), throughput 126
(my 83 chart + 43 shared in V-1).

**I thought I'd found a contradiction and I hadn't.** `prod_decorators=123` looked wrong against
my own AST scan of 129. The census is right and my scan was coarser: its matrix carries
`production_sites` / `test_sites` per id — **129 ids carry a `@register` anywhere, 123 have a
production site, 6 are registered only in test files** (e.g. `bad_infra_writer`). Doesn't touch
V-9: my reconciliation intersected with the registry, and none of the 6 is in it.

